{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And He called to Moses.</b> Always from within the cloud, as at Mount Sinai, as it says: וַיִּקְרָא אֶל מֹשֶׁה בַּיּוֹם הַשְּׁבִיעִי מִתּוֹךְ הֶעָנָן (Exodus 24:16), for he may never enter there without permission." "<b>From the Tent of Meeting.</b> For Moses had not yet entered the Tent of Meeting while the Glory was there. This was on the day Moses finished erecting the Mishkan, for then the Glory descended to sanctify the place and its ministers, as it says: וְנוֹעַדְתִּי שָׁמָּה לִבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל וְנִקְדַּשׁ בִּכְבֹדִי, וְקִדַּשְׁתִּי אֶת אֹהֶל מוֹעֵד וְאֶת הַמִּזְבֵּחַ וְאֶת אַהֲרֹן וְאֶת בָּנָיו (Exodus 29:43–44). So too He did in the Sanctuary of Solomon, as it says: וְלֹא יָכְלוּ הַכֹּהֲנִים לַעֲמֹד לְשָׁרֵת מִפְּנֵי הֶעָנָן כִּי מָלֵא כְבוֹד ה׳ אֶת בֵּית ה׳ (1 Kings 8:11), and thereby He sanctified the place, as it says: הִקְדַּשְׁתִּי אֶת הַבַּיִת הַזֶּה אֲשֶׁר בָּנִיתָ (1 Kings 9:3). But from the first day onward, Moses entered the Tent of Meeting outside the parokhet, and the speech came to him from above the kapporet, as it says: וּבְבֹא מֹשֶׁה אֶל אֹהֶל מוֹעֵד לְדַבֵּר אִתּוֹ וַיִּשְׁמַע אֶת הַקּוֹל מִדַּבֵּר אֵלָיו מֵעַל הַכַּפֹּרֶת (Numbers 7:89)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:35:49.148246502Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}